QuestGuidance.Register("en",131,{
[4161]="7002BFB4\n1\tDestroy avanc-nests (total: 6)\tAvanc-nests can be found at their breeding grounds, north-west of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore. Amal has asked you to destroy the avanc-nests in hopes of driving the creatures from the shores of the Limlight.\n2\tTalk to Amal at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore\tAmal is at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore, south-east of the avanc breeding grounds. You should return to Amal with news of your success.\n",
[4162]="7002BFAA\n1\tDefeat avanc in the Rushgore (total: 10)\tThe demons Amal spoke of, which sound suspiciously like avanc, wander the Rushgore. Amal asked you to banish the demons of the Rushgore to secure the safety of his party.\n2\tTalk to Amal at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore\tAmal is at the Woodman camp at the heart of the Rushgore. You should return to Amal and let him know that you have culled the number of avanc in the area.\n",
[4163]="7005B0E7\n1\tDefeat influenced goblins (total: 5)\tInfluenced goblins can be found in northern Gloomingtarn. You should defeat influenced goblins.\n2\tFurther explore where the influenced goblins are camped\tThe entrance to the Den of Pughlak can be found in the Gloomingtarn. You should further explore where the influenced goblins are camped.\n3\tComplete 'Den of Pughlak' on any difficulty\tComplete 'Den of Pughlak' on any difficulty. Use the Instance Finder to enter the Den of Pughlak.\n4\tTalk to Orti\tOrti can be found at Watchers' Roost in the Gloomingtarn. You should return to Watchers' Roost and talk to Orti.\n",
[4164]="7005B0CF\n1\tDelve deeper\tDelve deeper.\n2\tDefeat Kordkoth\tDefeat Kordkoth.\n3\tDelve deeper\tDelve deeper.\n4\tDefeat Pughlak\tDefeat Pughlak.\n",
[4165]="7005B0D6\n1\tDelve deeper\tDelve deeper.\n2\tDefeat Kordkoth\tDefeat Kordkoth.\n3\tDelve deeper\tDelve deeper.\n4\tDefeat Pughlak\tDefeat Pughlak.\n",
[4166]="7005B0D1\n1\tDelve deeper\tDelve deeper.\n2\tDefeat Kordkoth\tDefeat Kordkoth.\n3\tDelve deeper\tDelve deeper.\n4\tDefeat Pughlak\tDefeat Pughlak.\n",
[4167]="7005B0D3\n1\tDelve deeper\tDelve deeper.\n2\tDefeat Kordkoth\tDefeat Kordkoth.\n3\tDelve deeper\tDelve deeper.\n4\tDefeat Pughlak\tDefeat Pughlak.\n",
[4168]="7000795B\n1\tDefeat wolves at the wolf-den (total: 8)\tThe wolf-den is set in the cliff wall north-east of the lumber camp. Woodcutter Taylor Green is concerned that the wolves roaming the woods to the north-east may be a threat to the woodcutters and has asked you to cull their numbers.\n2\tTalk to Taylor Green\tWoodcutter Taylor Green waits at the lumber camp to the south-west, north of the guard-house. As Woodcutter Green requested, you put the fear of Men into the wolves of the Chetwood. He will be pleased to hear of your success.\n",
[4169]="700267F8\n1\tDefeat denizens of Ost Dunhoth (total: 100)\tOst Dunhoth is in southern Enedwaith. You have been asked to venture to Ost Dunhoth and defeat many of its denizens.\n2\tReturn to the Rangers of Thrór's Coomb\tThe Rangers in Thrór's Coomb will be pleased to hear you have culled some of Gortheron's forces.\n",
[4170]="7004DA34\n1\tDestroy Taurog-dens (total: 10)\tTaurog-dens can be found in Tholkát in northern Eryn Lasgalen. You should destroy Taurog-dens in Tholkát.\n2\tTalk to Thranduil\tThranduil can be found in Felegoth. You should talk to Thranduil.\n",
[4171]="7006C50B\n1\tDefeat Anâkhi cultists (total: 12)\tYour mission is to travel to Dul Râkh and stop the Anâkhi cultists there from producing more of their deadly poisons. If you can, slay their head apothecary Goródha as well.\n2\tGoródha has shown herself in Dul Râkh. Find and defeat her!\tGoródha has shown herself. You must defeat her to stop the Anâkhi's poison production!\n3\tFind and defeat Goródha\tGoródha has shown herself. You must defeat her to stop the Anâkhi's poison production!\n",
[4172]="700173B5\n1\tBring the crystals to Garthar at the Deep Descent\030Collect depleted crystals (total: 8)\tThe Forgotten Treasury is located south and south-east of the Deep Descent. Garthar asked you to search through the Forgotten Treasury for any sign of the depleted crystals within. Should you find them, he asked you to return them to him.\n",
[4173]="700571B4\n1\tGather fish from nets (total: 10)\030Gather nuts (total: 10)\tFish may be found in nets along a river in the Floodfells. You should gather any fish that you find.\n2\tPlace fish in a crate at Limlók\030Place nuts in a crate at Limlók\tA crate for the fish can be found in Limlók. You should put the fish in a crate.\n",
[4174]="70042EA7\n1\tSet traps in the northern forest (total: 4)\030Set traps in the northern forest area described by Derufin\030Set traps in the southern forest (total: 4)\030Set traps in the southern forest area described by Derufin\030Set traps in the eastern forest (total: 4)\030Set traps in the eastern forest area described by Derufin\tThe locations Derufin pointed to on his map can be found near Bâr Húrin. You should place traps in the wooded locations near Bâr Húrin that Derufin outlined on his map.\n2\tTalk to Derufin\tDerufin is located in Bâr Húrin. You should talk to Derufin.\n",
[4175]="7006AD8D\n1\tRestore badly desecrated tombs in Sektakhâb (total: 3)\030Restore desecrated tombs in Sektakhâb (total: 3)\tThe merchant Muntâkh has asked you to undo the desecration of tombs by grave robbers in Sektakhâb.\n2\tReturn to the merchant Muntâkh in Mekab-kuphâr\tReturn to the merchant Muntâkh in Mekab-kuphâr, the Temámir outpost in the southern Khabârkhad.\n",
[4176]="7001A49D\n1\tDefeat goblin-deserters in the Dourstocks (total: 3)\tGoblin-deserters can be found in the Dourstocks, between Echad Mothelen and Burgûl-stazg, to the north-west. Mothelen has asked you to hunt down some of the goblin-deserters and discover what has terrified them.\n2\tTalk to Mothelen at Echad Mothelen\tMothelen is at Echad Mothelen in the western Dourstocks, south-east of Burgûl-stazg. You should return to Mothelen with the information you have gathered.\n",
[4177]="70022CF1\n1\tEscort the drunken hobbit out of this public place\tDod Rumble is the disgrace of Budgford. Even the pigs behave better! You should escort the drunken hobbit to a secluded place where he won't be disturbing the good-mannered folk around town.\n2\tEscort the drunken hobbit out of this public place\tDod Rumble is the disgrace of Budgford. Even the pigs behave better! You should escort the drunken hobbit to a secluded place where he won't be disturbing the good-mannered folk around town. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[4178]="70022D80\n1\tEscort the drunken dwarf out of this public place\tPáll, a stranger who wandered down from Thrási's Lodge, is the disgrace of Celondim. You should escort the drunken dwarf to a secluded place where he won't be disturbing the good-mannered Elves around town. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[4179]="70022D82\n1\tEscort the drunken dwarf out of this public place\tAgmund is the disgrace of Duillond. You should escort the drunken dwarf to a secluded place where he won't be disturbing the good-mannered Elves around town. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[4180]="70022D81\n1\tEscort the drunken dwarf out of this public place\tNói is the disgrace of Needlehole. You should escort the drunken dwarf to a secluded place where he won't be disturbing the good-mannered folk around town. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[4181]="70022D59\n1\tEscort Robin Noakes out of this public place\tRobin Noakes is the disgrace of Stock, and that's saying a lot. No hobbit of Stock would be so attrocious at holding his beer. You should escort the drunken hobbit to a secluded place where he won't be making a fool of himself in front of the other patrons.\n2\tEscort Robin Noakes out of this public place\tRobin Noakes is the disgrace of Stock, and that's saying a lot. No hobbit of Stock would be so attrocious at holding his beer. You should escort the drunken hobbit to a secluded place where he won't be making a fool of himself in front of the other patrons. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[4182]="70022D58\n1\tEscort the drunken hobbit out of this public place\tAmaranth Goldworthy is the disgrace of Waymeet. You should escort the drunken hobbit to a secluded place where she won't be disturbing the good-mannered folk around town.\n2\tEscort the drunken hobbit out of this public place\tAmaranth Goldworthy is the disgrace of Waymeet. You should escort the drunken hobbit to a secluded place where she won't be disturbing the good-mannered folk around town. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[4183]="700304B6\n1\tFind the source of the rumour of Easterling siege-weapons\tThe rumours of an Easterling Woodyard point to the north-east of North-torr. You should locate this Woodyard and see what can be seen.\n2\tCollect siege-weapon designs (total: 2)\tThe Woodyard is north-east of North-torr. You should steal siege-weapon designs from the Woodyard.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have collected many siege-weapon designs to be shown later to Sergeant Guthferth.\n",
[4184]="7002F97B\n1\tAllow Ides to discuss her ambitions with you\tIdes can be found at the mill, north of the Rohirrim training grounds, at the northern edge of the Norcrofts. Ides has important matters on her mind that she wishes to discuss with you.\n2\tTalk to Ides\tIdes can be found at the mill, north of the Rohirrim training grounds, at the northern edge of the Norcrofts. Ides wishes to speak with you regarding the events at the training grounds.\n",
[4185]="70041864\n1\tSearch the ruins of Ethillorn for survivors\tEthillorn can be found to the south-west of Sarnhad in Lower Lebennin. Baraniel has asked you to search the sacked town of Ethillorn for any sign of survivors.\n2\tSearch deeper in Ethillorn for any sign of survivors\tEthillorn can be found to the south-west of Sarnhad in Lower Lebennin. You have searched near the entrance of Ethillorn, but have not yet found any survivors. You should now search deeper in Ethillorn.\n3\tEnslaved Gondorians can likely be found near the Corsair ships moored at Ethillorn. You have found one survivor in Ethillorn and he has begged your aid in freeing his folk from the Corsairs.\t\n4\tTalk to Baraniel in Sarnhad\tBaraniel can be found in Sarnhad in western Lower Lebennin. You have freed all the enslaved Gondorians you could, but not all were so fortunate. You should return to Baraniel in Sarnhad.\n",
[4186]="70044110\n1\tRally terrified soldiers and free civilians trapped by rubble\tYou must rally terrified soldiers and free civilians trapped by rubble.\n",
[4187]="700442CE\n1\tRally terrified soldiers and free civilians trapped by rubble\tYou must rally terrified soldiers and free civilians trapped by rubble.\n",
[4188]="7006C616\n1\tHold the Elf-stone aloft to inspire the Elf-twins\tGlorfindel asked you to hold the Elf-stone aloft near Elladan and Elrohir, who fight their enemies in the middle of the river to the north-west during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n2\tHold the Elf-stone aloft to inspire Legolas\tGlorfindel asked you to hold the Elf-stone aloft near Legolas, who fights on the western side of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n3\tHold the Elf-stone aloft to inspire Sigileth\tGlorfindel asked you to hold the Elf-stone aloft near Sigileth, who fights during the Dagor Carlanthir by the northern waterfall that hides Utug-bûr.\n4\tTalk to Sigileth during the Dagor Carlanthir\tSigileth fights beside Silirtas during the Dagor Carlanthir by the waterfall that hides Utug-bûr.\n5\tReturn the Elf-stone to Glorfindel during the Dagor Carlanthir\tGlorfindel fights to the south of Sigileth and Silirtas during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n",
[4189]="7006C618\n1\tGoblin-spies creep along the edges of the fighting during the Dagor Carlanthir.\t\n2\tDefeat goblin-spies during the Dagor Carlanthir (4/5)\tGoblin-spies creep along the edges of the fighting during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n3\tFind Balakhâd south of Mithrandir's position during the Dagor Carlanthir\tYou caught sight of Balakhâd fighting a goblin-spy to the south during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n4\tTalk to Balakhâd to the south of Mithrandir's position during the Dagor Carlanthir\tYou have found Balakhâd on the edge of the fighting during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n5\tWait for Balakhâd to escape\tOverwhelmed by the sight of such evil, Balakhâd flees from the battle.\n6\tTalk to Khôltekh during the Dagor Carlanthir\tKhôltekh is on the eastern bank of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n",
[4190]="7006C5EF\n1\tHurry to defend the waterfall north-west of Legolas\tLegolas asked you to stand your ground before the waterfall to the north-west.\n2\tDefend the north-west waterfall until time is up\tYou must defend the north-west waterfall and not leave it until enough time has passed! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Gimli during the Dagor Carlanthir\tGimli fights to the south-east during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n4\tHurry to defend the waterfall to Gimli's south-east\tGimli asked you to stand your ground at the waterfall to his south-east.\n5\tDefend the south-eastern waterfall until time is up\tYou must defend the waterfall to the south-east of Gimli, and not leave it until enough time has passed! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tTalk to Legolas during the Dagor Carlanthir\tLegolas fights during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n",
[4191]="7006C5EE\n1\tTalk to Girhâzi during the Dagor Carlanthir\tGirhâzi stands her ground north of her daughter during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n2\tDumûri warriors fight bravely during the Dagor Carlanthir.\t\n3\tTalk to Rahâzi to the south during the Dagor Carlanthir\tRahâzi fights to the south during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n",
[4192]="7006C617\n1\tPoint at Krazlak, the Orc-spymaster on the high ground above the western bank of the river\tRothog asked you to point at specific Orc spy-masters on the high ground to tell Húrshauk who to attack.\n2\tWait for Húrshauk to attack the target you indicated\tHúrshauk charges toward Krazlak!\n3\tPoint at Gadrúth, the Orc-spymaster on the high ground above the eastern bank of the river\tRothog asked you to point at specific Orcs on the high ground to tell Húrshauk who to attack.\n4\tWait for Húrshauk to attack the target you indicated\tHúrshauk charges toward Gadrúth!\n5\tTalk to Rothog during the Dagor Carlanthir\tRothog fights in the centre of the river during the Dagor Carlanthir.\n",
